<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lorvão Monastery</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Monastery of Lorvão is a former monastery near Penacova, north-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coimbra">Coimbra</a> in Portugal, one of the oldest in the country, with origins before the 10th century. A wealthy house of the Mozarabic frontier under the counts of Coimbra, it became a convent of Cistercian nuns in the early 13th century. Its scriptorium produced the Apocalypse of Lorvão of 1189, an illuminated copy of the Beatus commentary.</p></div>
